  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a VoiceOver user in Alertes Qualitay, I want to hear which alerts are new, as topic rows say « Non lu », so that the list tells me the same thing it shows.\n\n### Rule\n\n- \"Specify how elements are grouped, ordered, or linked. […] Examine your app for places where relationships among elements are visual only. Then, describe these relationships to VoiceOver.\" — [HIG › VoiceOver](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/voiceover).\n- \"Perceivable. Your interface doesn't rely on any single method to convey information.\" — [HIG › Accessibility](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/accessibility) (page updated 2025-06-09).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n`App/SwiftHFR/QualityAlerts/QualityAlertsView.swift:111-114`: `.scaledFont(.headline).bold(row.isNew).foregroundStyle(row.isNew ? .primary : .secondary)`, then `.accessibilityElement(children: .combine)` (`:124`) with no accessibility value. The headline is already semibold (`Settings/TextScale.swift:31`), so the weight step is only semibold to bold.\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\n`HFRswift/Swift/AQPlusView.swift:405-407`: `titleWeight: item.isNew ? .bold : .regular`, no accessibility text either. Shared gap; legacy's weight step (regular to bold) is larger.\n\n### Class\n\n**(a) defect**: accessibility, shared with legacy.\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- `.accessibilityValue(row.isNew ? \"Nouvelle\" : \"\")` on the row; regular weight for seen rows, as legacy.\n- Check: a hosted test on the row's accessibility value.\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
